    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: KVM: x86: Don't (re)check L1 intercepts when completing userspace I/O (CVE-2025-40026)\n\n* kernel: xen/privcmd: fix double free via VMA splitting (CVE-2026-31787)\n\n* kernel: gfs2: Fix use-after-free in iomap inline data write path (CVE-2026-45984)\n\n* kernel: Arm Processors: Privilege escalation or information disclosure via writes to higher exception level resources (CVE-2025-10263)\n\n* kernel: ipc: limit next_id allocation to the valid ID range (CVE-2026-52923)\n\n* kernel: net: openvswitch: reject oversized nested action attrs (CVE-2026-64531)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* qemu-kvm: error: failed to set MSR 0xc0000102 to 0xff4547ceb1600000 [RHEL.9.2.z] (JIRA:RHEL-126981)\n\n* [RHEL9.2-z] observe hang with nvme/051 test (JIRA:RHEL-129407)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
